Theorem DP-4: needs_sharing_observation truth table — Uniqueness = MaybeShared

  Preconditions:
    - s is a canonical AimsState per Annex E §AIMS product lattice
    - needs_sharing_observation : AimsState -> Bool per Annex E §AIMS DP-4 +
      Appendix C truth table
    - DP-4 is a pure boolean predicate over Uniqueness alone; Access /
      Consumption / Cardinality / Locality / Shape / Effect are
      non-load-bearing for the DP-4 obligation
    - Uniqueness carrier (Annex E §AIMS): {Unique, MaybeShared, Shared}
      with partial order Unique ≤ MaybeShared ≤ Shared
    - DP-4 is distinct from DP-5 / DP-9; DP-4 freezes an observation obligation;
      DP-5 + DP-9 compose Uniqueness with borrow_sources +
      project_alias_sources + IC-3 ParamContract.uniqueness for mutation
      obligation decisions

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState (canonical).
      needs_sharing_observation(s)
        <=> s.uniqueness = MaybeShared

    Unique: same-identity mutation can be admitted subject to DP-5.
    Shared: mutation isolation is mandatory.
    MaybeShared: sharing must be observed before selecting between those
      outcomes. The observation and isolation mechanisms are projection-owned.

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Exhaustive enumeration over the 3-value Uniqueness carrier per
          Appendix C truth table.
      (b) For each Uniqueness value, verify the predicate value equals the
          Appendix C row partition value AND verify exactly one row yields
          true (the MaybeShared row).

    Part (a) — Appendix C row partition (3 rows, exhaustive):
      Row 1: Uniqueness = Unique -> false (static unique fast path)
        Soundness: the one-owner outcome is statically known, so no additional
        sharing observation is required.
      Row 2: Uniqueness = MaybeShared -> true (dynamic sharing observation)
        Soundness: the observation determines logical owner multiplicity at
        the mutation point and selects the applicable neutral outcome.
      Row 3: Uniqueness = Shared -> false (static shared slow path)
        Soundness: multiple owners are statically known, so isolation is
        required without another sharing observation.

    Part (b) — negative-direction witness:
      DP-4 = true on EXACTLY the MaybeShared row; Unique and Shared both
      return false. The single-row partition is the gate-tightness witness.
      Coverage: 3 enumerated states; 1 true row; 2 false rows.

    DP-4 vs RL-6 / RL-7 / RL-8 mapping (downstream RC emission):
      DP-4 = false AND Uniqueness = Unique -> RL-6 same-identity outcome.
      DP-4 = true AND Uniqueness = MaybeShared -> RL-7 observation obligation.
      DP-4 = false AND Uniqueness = Shared -> RL-8 isolation obligation.
      The DP-4 truth table mechanically determines the mutation obligation
      per Annex E §AIMS RL-6 / RL-7 / RL-8.

    DP-4 vs DP-9 distinction:
      DP-4 is the BINARY observation-obligation predicate. DP-9 is the
      THREE-VALUE cow_mode classification (StaticUnique / StaticShared /
      Dynamic) that composes Uniqueness with DP-5 alias safety + IC-3
      ParamContract.uniqueness. DP-9 row (c) MaybeShared + IC-3.uniqueness =
      Unique -> StaticUnique can override the DP-4 = true verdict at the
      cow_mode classification layer; DP-4 itself remains the boolean
      observation-obligation gate evaluated PRIOR to DP-9 composition.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — 3-state enumeration over Uniqueness per
        section_05::verify_dp4_sharing_observation; the verifier checks the
        soundness equality on every Uniqueness value + asserts exactly 1
        row yields true)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_05 case_analysis engine discharges DP-4 via 3-state enumeration over Uniqueness; exactly the MaybeShared row requires a sharing observation
